1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.089
[S01] Collaboration and trust that didn't really exist in my schooling system.

2
00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.349
[S01] Although I think I turned out okay.

3
00:00:06.410 --> 00:00:07.280
[S02] You look okay.

4
00:00:07.309 --> 00:00:08.810
[S01] Yeah, I look okay.

5
00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.939
[S01] I think I had a couple of great teachers who were really motivating me and trusting me.

6
00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:13.679
[S02] Yeah.

7
00:00:13.710 --> 00:00:15.150
[S01] With what I was learning.

8
00:00:15.349 --> 00:00:18.010
[S01] So how do you regain trust in yourself as an adult?

9
00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:23.780
[S02] Well, first of all, you have to be aware, first thing, that, you know, you aren't trusting yourself.

10
00:00:24.179 --> 00:00:30.649
[S02] And you have to be aware of the fact that you're relying on other people's validation

11
00:00:30.989 --> 00:00:32.850
[S02] to make you feel good about yourself.

12
00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:37.560
[S02] And that puts you in a very dependent position.

13
00:00:37.899 --> 00:00:42.670
[S02] And if you don't get validated by other people all the time, then you get depressed.

14
00:00:43.140 --> 00:00:48.710
[S02] And the depression usually leads to alcohol or drugs or, you know,

15
00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.549
[S02] overly dependent on other people or other things.

16
00:00:53.079 --> 00:00:58.119
[S02] And so the first thing you need to do is to appreciate yourself

17
00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:03.560
[S02] and to stop blaming yourself all the time for everything that goes wrong.

18
00:01:03.630 --> 00:01:05.329
[S01] How, how do you do that?

19
00:01:05.359 --> 00:01:08.859
[S01] Because I was just, I was reading when I was preparing for this interview

20
00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:13.569
[S01] that you taught your daughters to be very easy with mistakes, like, and your students as well.

21
00:01:13.599 --> 00:01:14.739
[S01] Like, it's part of the process.

22
00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:17.840
[S02] Well, first of all, you need to realize that that's how you were brought up.

23
00:01:18.510 --> 00:01:23.010
[S02] And so that that's your natural instinct is to go back and blame yourself.

24
00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:23.409
[S01] Yeah.

25
00:01:23.750 --> 00:01:25.250
[S02] And then you have to stop it.

26
00:01:25.319 --> 00:01:27.620
[S02] You personally have to stop it.

27
00:01:27.879 --> 00:01:29.480
[S02] Stop blaming yourself.

28
00:01:29.879 --> 00:01:35.519
[S02] And, you know, that's, all these drug addicts that go to these, you know, rehab places.

29
00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:40.060
[S02] Do you know what, do you know what the success rate of those rehab centers is?

30
00:01:41.129 --> 00:01:44.129
[S02] 10%, 90% failure.

31
00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:50.909
[S02] And it's because they don't help those people understand themselves and believe in themselves.

32
00:01:51.170 --> 00:01:55.840
[S02] They're, they're just trying, it's kind of like trying to fix the problem without getting to the essence of it.

33
00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:02.620
[S02] Because they, all those people, they just, they feel bad about themselves.

34
00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.189
[S02] They learned that in childhood.

35
00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:07.219
[S02] That's why I focus on the childhood.

36
00:02:07.489 --> 00:02:13.430
[S02] Because, you know, we want the next generation of people to be happier,

37
00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.099
[S02] more supportive, more collaborative, kinder to each other.

38
00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:25.770
[S02] And we, we just need that because for the, for the world, we all need to work together on the climate issue.

39
00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:28.879
[S02] And we're not doing it now, as you noticed.

40
00:02:29.310 --> 00:02:32.379
[S02] And actually, it's somehow in the US, it's getting worse.

41
00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:33.580
[S01] Yeah, it's just tough.

42
00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:36.250
[S01] Exactly what you brought up, we were raised this way.

43
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:38.319
[S02] You were raised to beat yourself up.

44
00:02:38.349 --> 00:02:39.689
[S01] Why didn't you think more?

45
00:02:39.889 --> 00:02:40.520
[S02] That's right.

46
00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:42.189
[S01] Why didn't I think more?

47
00:02:42.590 --> 00:02:47.129
[S01] So next time, you probably won't make another step to improving your students.

48
00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:50.030
